From 54ace7c64773b6091fc7aa90d4997c0eeecf09cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AmirSalahY <hello@noury.ch>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 12:14:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 05/20] feat(ui): icon sets (nerd/unicode/emoji) + frosted
 glass menu styling
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the emoji icon column with real icons. Nerd Fonts are how a terminal
gets FontAwesome/Devicons/Codicons, so the default 'auto' resolves to those when
a patched font is installed and to single-cell geometric symbols otherwise —
never tofu, never the ragged column emoji caused (they are double-width, and the
variation-selector ones are measured inconsistently across terminals).

- theme.icons: auto | nerd | unicode | emoji | none, with IS_ICONS to override
  for a session. useNerdFont kept as a shorthand for existing rc files.
- Icons split into runtime/icons.ts: suggestion.ts sits in an import cycle, and
  the const export replacing the hoisted enum hit the temporal dead zone there.
- Icon column dimmed on unselected rows; rows composed per-segment so display
  width is measured before ANSI is applied.
- Two-tone border (lit top-left, shaded bottom-right) plus theme.surface, which
  defaults to 'clear' so the terminal's own transparency/blur is the frost.
- specs table now additionalProperties:false — a root key written below the
  [specs] header is TOML-scoped into it and was validating fine while being
  silently ignored, which is how maxSuggestions=10 sat dead.
- is doctor reports the resolved icon set and Nerd Font detection.
